Mode could be toggled mid-stream, causing tool execution enforcement to check a different mode than when the message was submitted. A message sent in Plan mode could execute tools if Tab was pressed during streaming.

## Changes

- **Block mode toggle during streaming**: Added `isStreaming` guard to `handleToggleMode()`, consistent with model picker, session picker, new chat, and history controls
- **Fix struct tag formatting**: Removed excess whitespace in `pkg/apis/cluster/v1alpha1/options.go` to satisfy golines linter

```go
func (m *Model) handleToggleMode() (tea.Model, tea.Cmd) {
    // Prevent mode mismatch between submission and tool execution
    if m.isStreaming {
        return m, nil
    }
    // ... toggle logic
}
```

Mode is now effectively locked when a message is submitted, ensuring tool enforcement matches user intent throughout the turn.

